  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="The Ritual of Kalgorath" id="0ca6-7a49-1d72-5c30" hidden="false">
      <description>The Matter of Kalgorath will never truly be lost, all must return to Tarcas. 

In your shooting phase, every OCCULT unit in your army with this rule that is not battle-shocked is eligible to preform a Ritual of Kalgorath. During this action, your OCCULT unit can select a nearby MATTER token within 9&quot;. Roll 3d6, if the result is higher than the units Ritual Difficulty, then it is a success. The dead unit&apos;s starting strength determines what Ritual Difficulty and Ritual Reward you receive. Upon success, select a Ritual Reward option. Upon a failure, the OCCULT unit suffers 1 mortal wound and the next OCCULT unit to attempt a Ritual of Kalgorath on the same MATTER token will receive a +1 to their roll (Stacks up to +3).


Starting Strength 0-9:
Ritual Difficulty: 6+ Ritual Rewards: 1 SP, Heal friendly unit in 9&quot; for d3 wounds, add d3 wounds to a Reforming Unit
Starting Strength 10-15:
Ritual Difficulty: 9+ Ritual Rewards: d2 SP, Heal friendly unit in 9&quot; for d3+1 wounds, add d6 wounds to a Reforming Unit
Starting Strength: 16-21
Ritual Difficulty: 12+ Ritual Rewards: 2 SP, Heal friendly unit in 9&quot; for d3+2 wounds, add d3+3 wounds to a Reforming Unit


Reforming Units:

When the Ritual of Kalgorath is successfully completed, you may start or add to a Reforming Unit. Select one unit that has died, a copy of that unit is placed in Strategic Reserves. CHARACTER units may not be reformed. You may then start adding wounds to said unit. If the unit has multiple models, once enough wounds are added to have one full model, the subsequent wounds move onto the next. The unit cannot be deployed from Strategic Reserves until they meet the minimum model requirements of that unit type. You may not have more than two Reforming Units at a time. Reforming Units are not affected by and do not affect your Strategic Reserve point limit. Once a Reforming Unit is deployed, it is no longer counted as a Reforming Unit.

For Beta Testing Purposes, here is a graph of starting strength based on a units total possible wounds.

Kalgorath - 16
Lagrashee - 6
Moribund - 4
Ordos - 5
Occultist - 3
Black wind Knights - 9/15/21 (Models: 3/5/7)
Cult Lackies - 10/20 (Models: 10/20)
Orc Lurkers - 10/20 (Models: 5/10)
Stone Golum - 10</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Children of Tarcas" id="3416-10b7-b72d-2a0e" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit dies, place a MATTER token as close to the center of the dead unit as possible</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
